msgstr ""

msgid "Model plots"
msgstr ""

msgid "Model plot"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Graphical representation of the estimated model, showing the factors "
"(circles), the indicators (squares) and the paths between them. Shown for "
"each group in a multigroup analysis."
msgstr ""

msgid "Misfit plots"
msgstr ""

msgid "Misfit plot"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Residual correlations between the indicators, i.e., the correlations that "
"remain unexplained by the model. Larger values indicate pairs of indicators "
"that the model reproduces poorly. Shown for each group in a multigroup "
"analysis."
msgstr ""

msgid "Model syntax"
msgstr ""

msgid "The lavaan model syntax that corresponds to the specified model."
msgstr ""

msgid "Average variance extracted"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Average variance extracted (AVE): the amount of variance that is captured by "
"a factor relative to the amount of variance due to measurement error. Values "
"above .5 are commonly taken to indicate adequate convergent validity."
msgstr ""

msgid "AVE"
msgstr ""

msgid "Heterotrait-monotrait ratio"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Heterotrait-monotrait (HTMT) ratio of correlations for assessing "
"discriminant validity between the factors. Values clearly below 1 (more "
"conservatively, below .85 or .90) suggest that the factors are empirically "
"distinct."
msgstr ""

msgid "Reliability"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Reliability of each factor and in total. Coefficient ω (omega) allows for "
"congeneric indicators (unequal loadings) and, with a second-order factor, is "
"also given for the second-order factor. Coefficient α (alpha) assumes tau-"
"equivalence (equal loadings). The total test score variance in the "
"denominator is the observed test score variance, i.e., the summed observed "
"covariance matrix. Values above .7 are commonly considered acceptable."
msgstr ""

